      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This affects both SDK2 and SDK3. The logic for checking if paths are the same is contained in VRCSdkControlPanelWorldBuilder.cs and starts at line 464. Reading the code, it goes through all Enabled objects (ignoring disabled objects) and for each of those, it loops through all sibling objects to find an object with the same name. There are no caching optimizations and the runtime is n^2 to check if any sibling has the same name. In large scenes, just switching to the build control tab can take 5 minutes to load, and changing to any other window and back restarts the timer. You cannot use your computer at all for this time if you want to build or upload your world.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
