  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-10-20T06:01:57.844Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When you have a large number of objects all under the same parent, the Build Control panel becomes extremely laggy. \nIn my scene, I have 2048 objects, each with a vrc_trigger. Switching to the build control panel takes 80 seconds and allocates over 2gb. Attached screenshot is a deep profile of the editor. \nSort of related, but disabling the parent of these objects \"fixes\" the lag. I assume this means that any checks the sdk tries to do ignores disabled objects.",
